`taiga-mcp-server` now requires an explicit `serve` subcommand to start the MCP server. Running the bare command with no subcommand no longer starts it (it shows the command list instead) - update any MCP client configuration invoking it with no arguments to add ` serve`. `taiga.mcp_server.cli.main()`'s signature also changed, from `main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int` to `main() -> None` - this only affects code calling `main()` directly, not the `taiga-mcp-server` console script.
